%rec: OpeningBranch

# Solara "Binary" Carter
# Role: Tech Specialist and Hacker
# - (techie, false prophet for a noble goal, dreamer for the stars)

# She wants to believe in the good but people are continually disappointing her. Now she only trusts in logic and tech.

# She is an actually funny kind of nerd, but she would also be willing to just leave earth behind any time. She doesn’t like it here. Always felt like she didn’t belong.

# The idea with the moon colony came originally from her, but Dex blatantly stole it from her and made it his own.

# She has a quirk of using tech terms in her everyday language.

cond: true
goto: DefaultIntroduction

cond: HasFlag('IntroducedTo(solara_carter)')

%rec: Nodes

name: DefaultIntroduction
npc: Twenty-two hundred, Solara Carter.
+ Extended Simple Mail Transfer Service Ready.
#
o_text: Hi, Solara. Nice to meet you.
o_id: hi_solara
o_goto: HiSolara
#
o_text: Uhm, what? Are you a computer?
o_goto: What
#
o_text: HELO, {{ .pcname }}.
o_cond: Skill('Technology') >= 15
o_goto: Helo
#
o_text: EHLO, {{ .pcname }}.
o_cond: Skill('Technology') >= 25
o_goto: Ehlo
#
o_text: I better be going.
o_goto: Bye

## Default EXIT Begin

## Default EXIT End

## Default Character Questions Begin

name: HiSolara
npc: Aw, well. Hi there. What can I do for you?
#
o_text: I am a contractor, offering my services.
o_goto: ContractorOffer
#
o_text: What is this place?
o_goto: WhatIsThisPlace
#
o_text: What do you do here?
o_goto: WhatDoYouDo
#
o_text: Tell me about yourself.
o_goto: TellMeAboutYourself
#
o_text: What are your thoughts on EBI?
o_goto: ThoughtsOnEBI
#
o_text: What do you think about BAT?
o_goto: ThoughtsOnBAT
#
o_text: What can you tell me about Flesh & Bone?
o_goto: FleshAndBone
#
o_text: I hear you sell tickets. The golden kind.
o_id: ask_ticket
o_goto: Ticket
#
o_text: I have the spaceport manifest. Zero berths, every hull.
o_id: sell_manifest
o_cond: HasItem('spaceport_manifest') && !HasFlag('dead_freight(public)')
o_goto: BuyManifest


name: Bye
npc: Connection closed by remote host. See you around, {{ .pcname }}.
effect: EndConversation

name: What
npc: (She grins.) No, I just talk like one before my second coffee.
+ Solara Carter. I keep the machines in this district from eating people.
effect: SetFlag('IntroducedTo(solara_carter)')
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: Helo
npc: Oh, a person who reads RFCs. HELO accepted, {{ .pcname }}.
+ You have no idea how rare that is around here.
effect: SetFlag('IntroducedTo(solara_carter)')
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: Ehlo
npc: Extended handshake, even. Alright, you have my attention.
+ Most people around here think a protocol is something you break.
effect: SetFlag('IntroducedTo(solara_carter)')
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: ContractorOffer
npc: A contractor. So, a person-shaped script someone else runs.
+ No offense. I might have a job for you eventually, if you don't turn out to be a liability.
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: WhatIsThisPlace
npc: The eastern rim. Officially a commerce district.
+ Practically, it's where the two big corps park the things they don't want on their own campus.
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: WhatDoYouDo
npc: I fix what breaks. Terminals, drones, the odd cyberdeck.
+ And I listen to the traffic nobody thinks I can read.
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: TellMeAboutYourself
npc: Not much to report. I was going to put people on the moon.
+ Someone with a better suit filed my idea under his own name, so now I'm here, fixing vending machines.
+ Machines don't do that to you. That's why I like them.
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: ThoughtsOnEBI
npc: Eschaton Biotech? They own the water you drink and the doctor who tells you it's fine.
+ I'd rather not be on their network. Or their list.
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: ThoughtsOnBAT
npc: Bushido-ArmaTech at least admit what they sell.
+ There's a kind of honesty in a weapons company. Not one I want to work for, mind you.
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: FleshAndBone
npc: Purity of the flesh. (She taps the interface port behind her ear.)
+ To them I'm not a person, I'm a violation. So we don't talk much.
+ If you have chrome in you, don't go east after dark.
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

## Package B: ticket seller and buyer of the manifest (Dead Freight, outcome 'buried')

name: Ticket
npc: I handle the bookings for the eastern rim, yes. One million sat, one berth, one way. Up.
+ (She pats the terminal.) Payment clears, your name goes on the list. The list is long.
effect: SetFlag('KnowsAbout(golden_ticket)')
#
effect: ReturnToPreviousNode

name: BuyManifest
npc: (She reads it without touching it.) Where did you... no. Don't tell me.
+ Listen. If this gets out, a thousand people learn they are going to die here instead of somewhere else. Same death, less hope.
+ Eight hundred sat and it never existed. Shaw gives you five, I checked.
#
o_text: Eight hundred. It never existed.
o_id: bury_manifest
o_goto: Buried
#
o_text: Keep your money.
o_id: refuse_bury
o_goto: HiSolara

name: Buried
npc: (The printout goes into the shredder in one motion.) Transaction complete. Exit code zero.
+ Go on believing whatever you believed before you walked in.
effect: StackTransferTo(NPC, 'spaceport_manifest')
effect: PlayerAddGold(800)
effect: SetFlag('dead_freight(buried)')
#
o_text: Sure.
o_id: buried_bye
o_goto: Bye
